ANALYTICS PROJECTS
Predictive Medical Diagnostic System using Advanced Ensemble ML  —  2025
Python · scikit-learn · XGBoost · LightGBM · CatBoost · LDA · PCA · VIF · Stratified CV · Stacking
•	Built end-to-end multinomial classification pipeline predicting 41 diseases from 132 binary symptoms across 
  304 deduplicated patient records; resolved severe multicollinearity (63 highly correlated symptom pairs) 
  via two-stage hierarchical clustering and iterative VIF elimination, reducing the feature space by 30% while 
   retaining maximum discriminative signal.
•	Applied and empirically compared five dimensionality reduction strategies 
   (PCA, LDA, TruncatedSVD, VIF-filtered, Hybrid) — Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA) outperformed all others
    by projecting 132 features into 40 supervised discriminant components that directly maximise separation across 
   41 disease classes, confirming its theoretical optimality for multinomial targets.
•	Engineered 25+ domain-driven features including 10 clinical symptom group scores 
     (gastro, neuro, cardiac, respiratory, hepatic), symptom rarity-weighted signals, Shannon entropy of symptom
     distribution, and multi-organ system breadth index — capturing diagnostic patterns invisible to raw binary inputs.
•	Trained and intensively tuned 7 advanced ensemble models (Random Forest, XGBoost multi:softmax, LightGBM, CatBoost, 
     Extra Trees, Soft Voting, Stacking with multinomial LR meta-learner) using RandomizedSearchCV (40–60 iterations each)
     with Stratified 5-Fold CV; applied class_weight=‘balanced’ throughout — no SMOTE — to handle post-dedup class imbalance.
•	Achieved ~97% weighted F1 (cross-validated) and ~0.99 ROC-AUC (OvR macro) across 41 disease categories;
    evaluated with per-class F1, macro F1, weighted precision/recall, and One-vs-Rest ROC curves,
    demonstrating robust generalisation on a high-difficulty 41-class multinomial problem with limited training data (304 rows).
